    "Town homepage identifies Luzerne County and Drums address and announces a temporary outage; only recent documents are linked. Treat this as an archive-access limitation, not evidence of legal repeal or absence of records.",
    "November10 agenda lists approval of October13 public-hearing/general minutes; its own three proposed ordinances concern speed limits and road names, not data centers. November3 work session and November2 planning agenda do not document an October13 adoption or termination. They are agendas, not completed minutes.",
    "The retained Times Leader article dated October13 reports ordinance adoption after a Tuesday hearing, special-exception use in Industrial zoning and possible future conditional-use amendment. It links the narrative to the May12 curative process. This supports attributed reporting, not authenticated enacted text or exact termination/effect dates.",
    "Article includes both600foot sensitive-receptor separation and resident discussion of1250foot setbacks. Do not silently reconcile or promote detailed controlling thresholds without the ordinance.",
    "A third-party tracker assigns October19 to the same report. Use the original article dateline for attribution, not the tracker date. Keep Luzerne County distinct from Butler County and Schuylkill County/Highridge actions."
  ],
